   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "A particle moves along a line, and its position, in centimeters, is \\( s(t) = - 4 t^{2} - 4 t + 1 \\) for time t in seconds. At what rate is the position of the particle changing at the instant t = 3 seconds?",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": -28
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "An average rate is available over any interval, so take the short interval from t = 3 to t = 3 + h. The average rate over it is \\( \\frac{s(3 + h) - s(3)}{h} \\).",
         "rule_named": "average rate of change over a short interval"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Expanding and dividing by h leaves \\( \\frac{s(3 + h) - s(3)}{h} = - 4 h - 28 \\), which still depends on the length h of the interval.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Multiply",
               -1,
               4,
               "h"
            ],
            -28
         ],
         "rule_named": "difference quotient simplified"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The rate at the instant is what these averages approach as h approaches 0: \\( \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{s(3 + h) - s(3)}{h} = -28 \\). This limit is the derivative \\( s'(3) \\).",
         "mathjson": -28,
         "rule_named": "limit of the difference quotient"
      }
   ],
